abstract: >-
  LLM Council is a multi-LLM tool that generates JUnit 5 unit tests for Java
  classes using several language models, runs a blind peer review and vote
  between them, synthesizes a consensus "winner" test suite, and measures
  quality with JaCoCo line/branch coverage and PIT mutation testing — all
  through a local Flask backend and a browser UI. It is provider-agnostic:
  contributors bring their own API key and gateway (BYOK).
keywords:
  - software-testing
  - large-language-models
  - unit-testing
  - junit
  - mutation-testing
  - code-coverage
